# Innovatech PH — Campus Navigation Product Spec

The old NU Museum codebase in this folder is the **legacy system**. The new product is:

**AI-Assisted AR 360° Virtual Campus Navigation and Information System for Educational Institutions**

Reusable PHP + MySQL + JavaScript + A-Frame product for Innovatech PH, customizable per school client.

Do not remove, skip, or silently shrink any feature below when designing schema, UI, or code.

## Roles

| Role | Scope |
|------|--------|
| **owner** | Platform (Innovatech). Landing page of the product, roles, logs, access, emails, system setup/config, institutions. Creates admin accounts and organizations. |
| **admin** | One (or assigned) institution. Manages that school's 360 / AR / VR tour content, org settings, themes, landing mode, starting point, visual file environment. Not a coder — edits via drag-and-drop / visual tools. |
| **staff** | Under an admin + institution. Updates information, images, floor plans, featured tour images, facilities, AI stitch/capture. Same visual tools as admin for content, not platform config. |
| **user** | View-only. Students, applicants, visitors. Explore 360 tours, floor-plan landing, and live AR walk. |

## Organization / project folders

- Owner creates the **admin** role and the **institution**.
- Creating an institution **generates a new project folder** with template files (A-Frame 360 landing, assets, theme stubs).
- Admin then configures the organization (mode, starting point, theme).
- Admin/staff must **not** need to edit code. Provide a visual environment: drag-and-drop 360 scenes, markers, floor-plan pins, popups, infographics, animations.

## Institution landing modes (exactly two)

1. **360_rotation** — Full-screen A-Frame 360 (see legacy `vtour.php` as UX reference: full-screen rotating capture). Starts at the **starting scene** set by admin.
2. **floor_plan** — Uploaded campus floor-plan image is the landing. Circular buttons are **drag-and-dropped** onto the image. Clicking a pin opens that location's tour/info.

Admin/staff choose which mode is the main landing.

## Floor plans — strict responsive sizing

- Floor-plan markers **must use percentage (or 0–1) coordinates**, never raw pixels as the source of truth.
- Store original image width/height and lock aspect ratio (`object-fit: contain`).
- Image and markers must stay aligned on every screen size. Do not let layout “break” the plan.
- Mobile landing AR / 360 must be **landscape full-screen**.

## Content model (per institution)

- Buildings, rooms, campus areas, facilities.
- 360 scenes + room-to-room hotspots (connected locations).
- Featured images for tours.
- Facility descriptions (manual + **AI-assisted** generation).
- Themes: colors, popup animations, infographic look.

## AI stitch / capture tools (admin + staff)

Two intake paths, both produce a stitchable cubemap / equirectangular panorama:

1. **Upload cubemap** (faces).
2. **Capture in-system** with guides: top / left / right / down / front / back (mobile panorama-style). Capture may be messy; **AI stitch** still processes it.

Job status, source faces, and output panorama must be persisted.

## AR (do not drop)

- Overlay digital information, directions, labels, interactive content on real campus views.
- **Walk-with-camera** (Google Maps Live View style): user walks on campus; system detects they are at a mapped area.
- Detection inputs include: floor-plan marker points (same drag-and-drop pins) **and** AR-captured / geo waypoints for that area.
- Map floor-plan pins ↔ real-world location (lat/lng and/or visual/AR target).

## Multi-school

Schema and folders are tenant-scoped by `institution_id`. Innovatech deploys many school clients from one product.

## Stack

PHP, MySQL, JavaScript, A-Frame (360/AR web), AI services where appropriate.

The Innovatech PH **product landing** is PHP (`landing/index.php`), not React. Owner manages copy/settings (`platform_settings`). Do not reintroduce Next.js for this page.

## Schema file

Canonical SQL: `database/schema.sql`. Extend it rather than inventing parallel tables.
